<% content_for :title, "MTU" %>

<div class="w-full max-w-6xl mx-auto space-y-4">

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        My Traveller Universe
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3  text-slate-100">
        Traveller Referees can use this site to manage sectors and star systems that their Travellers will encounter
        of the course of a
        <%= link_to "Deepnight Revelation",
                    "https://www.mongoosepublishing.com/products/deepnight-revelation-core-set",
                    target: "_blank",
                    rel: "noopener noreferrer",
                    class: "underline hover:text-traveller-red hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2"
        %> campaign. You can start with a blank star map, adding sectors and star systems as you wish. You can also start
        with a prepopulated star map of uncharted space with 135 sectors and over 36,000 star systems generated using
        the rules from
        <%= link_to "World Builder's Handbook",
          "https://www.mongoosepublishing.com/products/world-builders-handbook",
          target: "_blank",
          rel: "noopener noreferrer",
          class: "underline hover:text-traveller-red hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2"
        %>
        .</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-100">You can track the progress of the Revelation through uncharted space and
        present a digital map to the Travellers.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-100">My Traveller Universe integrates with
        <%= link_to "Traveller Map",
                    "https://travellermap.com",
                    target: "_blank",
                    "rel": "noopener noreferrer",
                    class: "underline hover:text-traveller-red hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2"
        %> so you can generate hex maps of the sectors.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-100">This site was created under Mongoose Publishing's
        <%= link_to "Fair Use Policy",
                    fairuse_path,
                    class: "underline hover:text-traveller-red hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2"
        %></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
